  "private": true,
  "//op-sqlite": [
    "Compile-time switch, read by node_modules/@op-engineering/op-sqlite/op-sqlite.podspec",
    "(line 55) and the Android CMake equivalent. It swaps the bundled stock SQLite",
    "amalgamation for SQLCipher's and defines OP_SQLITE_USE_SQLCIPHER=1.",
    "",
    "Changing this REQUIRES a native rebuild -- pod install + expo run:ios. Metro",
    "reloads will not pick it up. Without the flag, the encryptionKey passed in",
    "lib/powersync/db.ts is accepted and silently ignored, and every note is stored",
    "in the clear. lib/powersync/migrateToEncrypted.ts asserts isSQLCipher() at",
    "startup so that misconfiguration fails loudly instead."
  ],
  "op-sqlite": {
    "sqlcipher": true
  },
  "allowScripts": {
    "fsevents@2.3.3": true,
    "unrs-resolver@1.12.2": true,
    "sharp@0.28.0": true
  },
  "//overrides.@10play/tentap-editor": [
    "tentap declares react-dom ^18.2.0 as a hard dependency, so npm nests its own",
    "18.3.1 while the rest of the tree dedupes onto 19.1.0. expo doctor fails the",
    "duplicate-native-module check on that, which fails the EAS build.",
    "",
    "It is also incoherent on its own terms: react and react-dom must share a major,",
    "and tentap was pairing react 19 (hoisted) with react-dom 18. Harmless on native,",
    "where react-dom never loads -- the editor is a prebuilt web bundle inside a",
    "WebView -- but it would bite on the web platform.",
    "",
    "Scoped under the package name rather than written bare like the four below, so",
    "the rewrite is confined to tentap's subtree and nothing else silently changes",
    "resolution."
  ],
  "overrides": {
    "@10play/tentap-editor": {
      "react-dom": "19.1.0"
    },
    "lightningcss": "1.30.1",
    "nativewind": "^5.0.0-preview.4",
    "postcss": "^8.5.11",
    "uuid": "^11.1.1"
  },
  "resolutions": {
    "lightningcss": "1.30.1"
  }
}
